<urn:usf:acceptance:hermes-linear-autonomy> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Place the direct Linear CLI adapters and delivery orchestration in the existing commands interface component. Preserve the declared operations-to-interface and operations-to-realisation dependency prohibitions; retire the misplaced continuous delivery coordinator and unowned linear module paths through exact candidate deletions. No architecture exception or weakened corpus conformance is permitted. Use only policy-selected https://api.linear.app/graphql with explicit per-workspace credential names and api-key or bearer authentication. Verify organization URL key and exact team UUID before issue discovery or mutation. Credentials remain in one explicit owner-private repository credential file and never reach provider or validation processes. Bound request timeout, response bytes, pagination, repeated cursors and rows; any incomplete discovery prevents completion detection. Linear text, assignment and status are coordination only. Derive selected work from exact current graph-owned LinearIssueWorkBinding records and preserve superseded attempts. Discovered unbound issues are explicitly blocked, never interpreted as source, shell commands or execution authority. New coordination issues require exact graph-authored proposal identity, owner/team, title and description; creation alone never activates a WorkPacket. Persist exact mutation intent before contact with immutable payload digest and stable client-generated remote UUID. Authenticate remote issue/team and intended state or comment body on readback before recording success. Preserve STARTED/UNKNOWN after interruption; reconcile the exact remote identity and never retransmit an unknown mutation merely because a search returned zero rows. Reject conflicting identities and unsafe files; use private atomic durable writes and existing process/activity exclusion. hermes start --linear-policy IRI --manifest PATH owns a foreground autonomous loop under the existing supervisor lifetime lock and activity exclusion. start/status/stop need no external Codex, Claude or human controller loop. Observe exact Linux process identity, bounded drain and pending transactions, release kernel ownership on exit, and reconstruct from current graph plus persisted intents/results on restart. Preserve the legacy lifecycle when the opt-in selector is absent. Prepare current bindings and execute using shared Hermes/USF route selection. Admit only authenticated settled operation-bearing results with exact RealisationBasis, current scoped preimages, known required provider identity and real available usage/economic/qualification evidence. Resolve/apply/check/integrate through existing handlers; after integration rederive construction currentness and execute ordinary completion evidence/proof/publication. Never fabricate missing lineage, usage, qualified capacity or a successful completion. Use shared catalogue, economics, privacy, capabilities, context limits, current task-class qualification and persisted route health/deferrals. No named model family is required or preferred by this lane. Refresh health or qualification only through graph-authorized bounded existing commands. Preserve exact qualifying record digests in dispatch evidence. Provider failures advance to other qualified routes and block only work with no eligible route; tests and a separate live run disable Codex/Claude and exercise alternatives. Provider child invocation uses an explicit contained USF_PROVIDER_HOME and an explicit sanitized child environment at the process boundary, never ambient operator HOME or Linear credentials. Capability observation and invocation select the same contained identity root. Refuse unsafe or absent provider-home authority; do not copy credentials, alter the parent environment or touch unrelated sessions. Rank actionable issues deterministically by priority with bounded fair progress and preserve pending attempts. A blocked item produces evidence and a deduplicated remote comment or policy-selected blocked state and cannot stop independent ready work. Done requires current published semantic completion and exact remote readback. Whole-scope completion requires complete discovery, every relevant issue accounted for, no pending/unknown mutation or work attempt, and zero actionable work; all-blocked is distinct from completed. Offline tests exercise actual client request construction through injected transports, wrong workspace/team, partial GraphQL errors, pagination bounds, create/update/comment readback, interruption and duplicate prevention, missing credential before contact, current completion-only Done, independent blocked continuation, provider failover, and real CLI lifetime/status/stop behavior. Fixtures cannot establish live API/provider behavior; full authoritative check remains required." <urn:usf:graph:hermes-linear-autonomy> .
